hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1780","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Hell will be thrown into Hell, and Hell will say, 'Are there any more? (i.e., throw more, throw more)' until Allah places His Foot over it, then Hell will say, 'Enough, enough.'"
"1781","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Hell and Paradise argued with each other. Hell said, ‘I have been designated for punishing the arrogant and the tyrants.’ Paradise said, ‘I do not know what is the reason that only the poor, needy, and those looked down upon will enter me.’ Allah Almighty said to Paradise: ‘You are My mercy; among My righteous servants, I will bestow mercy through you upon whom I will.’ And He said to Hell: ‘You are the place of My punishment; among My servants, I will punish through you whom I will.’ And for each of them, a limit has been set for filling them, but Hell will not be filled until Allah Almighty places His foot upon it. At that time, Hell will say, ‘Enough, enough,’ and then it will be filled and will contract. As for Paradise, Allah Almighty will create another creation for it (so that Paradise may be filled with that creation).”"
